    "Buchwald"
   ],
   "year": 2025,
   "journal": "Acta Geotechnica 20:1621-1642",
   "doi": "10.1007/s11440-024-02502-w"
  },
  "dimension": 2,
  "physics_class": "thermal (conduction-only leg of the THM benchmark)",
  "validation_method": "Digitized temperature histories at observation points P1-P4, Fig. 7, all SEVEN participating codes (ANDRA COMSOL / ANDRA Code_Aster / BGE OpenGeoSys / EDF Code_Aster / LEI COMSOL / ULg LAGAMINE / UPC Code_Bright)",
  "validation_target": "T(P1) rises 22 degC to ~75 degC after 10 y at 200 W/m; T(P4) ~40 degC (Boom fig.); overlay on paper day axis",
  "notes": "Conduction-only is NOT an approximation here: the benchmark's own code comparison (Tab. 7) shows FLAC3D omits advective transport with negligible T deviation - at k=2.3e-20 m2 advection is negligible. Anisotropic case NOT reproducible (isotropic lambda only). Heating starts at t=183.6 d (86400 s excavation + 6 months waiting) via Neumann start_time, so curves align with the paper's day axis."
 },
